From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: call the built-in EN751221 WHNAT hook directly

mt76_rx_complete() looked up en75_whnat_upstream_early with symbol_get()
and dropped it with symbol_put() on every NAPI poll. Each lookup is a
binary search with strcmp over the kernel's exported symbols plus a
module reference: about 1.6 % of the RX CPU during a WiFi upload on the
XR500v. WHNAT is built into the kernel there (CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_WHNAT=y),
so the symbol is always present: call it directly and keep the lookup
only for a modular build.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -1562,7 +1562,10 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
-#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_WHNAT)
+#if IS_BUILTIN(CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_WHNAT)
+	/* Built in: no lookup needed (a symbol_get() per poll costs ~2 %). */
+	whnat_early = en75_whnat_upstream_early;
+#elif IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_WHNAT)
 	/* Looked up once per poll; the hook keeps the frames it takes. */
 	whnat_early = symbol_get(en75_whnat_upstream_early);
 #endif
@@ -1572,7 +1575,7 @@
 			continue;
 		napi_gro_receive(napi, skb);
 	}
-#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_WHNAT)
+#if IS_MODULE(CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_WHNAT)
 	if (whnat_early)
 		symbol_put(en75_whnat_upstream_early);
 #endif
